# 1Password references for pi (https://pi.dev) API keys.
#
# This file is sourced by `op run --env-file` via the `pi` shell wrapper
# defined in ~/.zshrc. Values use 1Password secret references
# (op://<vault>/<item>/<field>) — no plaintext secrets live here.
#
# Setup: create a 1Password item named "pi-keys" in vault "Private"
# with fields matching the variable names below, then uncomment the
# providers you actually use.

# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=op://Private/pi-keys/ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
# OPENAI_API_KEY=op://Private/pi-keys/OPENAI_API_KEY
# GEMINI_API_KEY=op://Private/pi-keys/GEMINI_API_KEY
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=op://Private/pi-keys/OPENROUTER_API_KEY
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=op://Private/pi-keys/DEEPSEEK_API_KEY
# GROQ_API_KEY=op://Private/pi-keys/GROQ_API_KEY
# XAI_API_KEY=op://Private/pi-keys/XAI_API_KEY
